15. AS/STUDENT/TEACHER RESUME ATOMICITY AND ALL-RANK CONTRACT CLOSURE
======================================================================

The post-snapshot audit continued through the exact student, teacher, AS, and
distributed save/resume paths. These changes remain workspace-only and are not
part of the immutable, already-running r21 source snapshot.

Actor noise state and student/teacher correctness:

- A finite but invalid checkpoint actor `std` could previously be copied into
  a live actor and then silently projected by `_sanitize_actor_std`. Full
  resume, actor-only policy init, and strict teacher load now compare the saved
  tensor with the exact pure runtime projection before any module mutation and
  reject any value that would change.
- The projection order had a real edge-case error: an oversized component
  could make the pre-cap mean appear above `min_mean_noise_std`, then the final
  cap could leave the effective mean below the requested floor. The common
  projection now applies the component cap before evaluating the mean floor;
  `[2.0, 0.1]` with mean floor/cap `0.8` correctly becomes `[0.8, 0.8]`.
- `init_noise_std`, `min_noise_std`, `min_mean_noise_std`, and `max_noise_std`
  must now be finite and positive when present. Component and mean floors are
  explicitly mutually exclusive, removing the former truthiness-dependent
  interpretation of zero or contradictory settings.
- Strict teacher loading now requires a parseable serialized actor config,
  recursively finite actor state, prevalidated module compatibility, and a
  valid saved `std`. The intentional non-strict extra-input compatibility path
  validates every shared tensor before loading instead of relying on a failed
  `load_state_dict` that may already have partially copied parameters.
- Teacher observation normalizers are validated across every alias before any
  alias is loaded: exact keys/shapes/dtypes/layouts, finite values,
  non-negative count/variance, positive std, and std/variance/eps consistency.
  Thus one bad late alias cannot leave earlier aliases partially restored.

Adaptive-sampler resume contract:

- `AdaptiveTimestepsSampler.state_dict()` is now version 3 and records
  `adaptive_kernel_size`, `adaptive_lambda`, `adaptive_uniform_ratio`, and
  `adaptive_alpha`. Version-3 restore compares all four exactly. Versions 1/2
  predate these fields and are accepted only when the runtime uses the
  historical production defaults `(1, 0.8, 0.1, 0.001)`; non-default legacy
  restores fail closed.
- The v1 failure-only migration previously assigned unit exposure to every
  valid bin. Legitimate old failure EMAs greater than one would load but fail
  at the next probability calculation. Migration now uses a clip-wise constant
  `max(1, max_failure)` exposure, preserving relative legacy priorities while
  satisfying `failure <= exposure`. A `[2, 4]` repro migrates to exposure
  `[4, 4]` and produces finite normalized probabilities.

Distributed checkpoint atomicity:

- Fixed-BC save no longer evaluates rank-local state before its collective.
  Every rank, including a zero-budget rank, first joins the real all-rank Gloo
  envelope with its actual group rank/world, state or error, and runtime
  allocation fingerprint. Local serialization/contract failures are reported
  identically by all ranks after the gather rather than stranding peers.
- The fingerprint covers allocation version/scheme, global budget, world size,
  rank/local quotient-remainder target, and DAgger enablement. Resume validates
  the same fingerprint and rejects unknown actions or a `noop` mixed with
  `restore/clear`; an explicit reset requested by any rank still becomes one
  global reset plan.
- Budget parsing and fingerprint construction themselves are inside the error
  envelope. Tests force those functions to raise and prove
  `all_gather_object` is still called exactly once. Environment-state save was
  hardened analogously so a rank-local serialization/non-finite error cannot
  leave other ranks blocked in its object gather.

Validation evidence after the final delta:

- Broad student/teacher/PPO/AS/resume/preflight/provenance suite:
  `420 passed, 1 skipped`.
- Focused fixed-BC collective suite: `26 passed`.
- Full launcher contracts passed, including transactional rollback, ownership
  and FD boundaries, MuJoCo perception metadata, and content-addressed source
