19. POST-SNAPSHOT SEED, RNG, AND CHECKPOINT-BYTE INTEGRITY
======================================================================

The fresh-run boundary was moved after W&B initialization, distributed
barriers, and final asset preflight, immediately before environment
construction.  `PYTHONHASHSEED` and `CUBLAS_WORKSPACE_CONFIG` are now set and
validated before importing torch/CUDA-facing modules.  Base seed, maximum
global-rank offset, topology, and the uint32 upper bound are checked before
Python, NumPy, torch CPU/CUDA, simulator, or Warp RNG state can be mutated.
The batch launcher forwards the canonical seed through every independent
remote shell and the terminal distill command consumes it as exactly one
`--training.seed` argument.  Seed/hash/CUBLAS settings are recorded in
training provenance and compared on resume.

Lazy student modules are materialized before model broadcast and optimizer
construction.  Materialization preserves and restores Python, NumPy, torch
CPU, and torch CUDA RNG state even on failure, and optimizer coverage is
checked for every trainable parameter.  Checkpoints now serialize rank-local
RNG state.  Exact continuation includes curriculum and process RNG state, but
the production configuration still uses non-deterministic CUDA/TF32 settings;
it supports statistical reproducibility, not a bitwise trajectory claim.

Every production checkpoint reader used by training, eval, inference, batch,
AS, terrain, Viser, and MuJoCo routes through the shared safe loader.  It opens
a regular file with `O_NOFOLLOW`, hashes and deserializes the same file
descriptor with `weights_only=True`, compares identity and SHA256 before and
after load, and can require the provenance-authenticated digest.  No direct
production `torch.load` call remains outside that loader.  Hostile-pickle,
symlink, mutation, wrong-digest, and schema regressions passed.

These contracts are workspace-only.  Formal r21 predates `rng_state_by_rank`;
the new code therefore rejects an r21 checkpoint as an exact deterministic
resume unless `ALLOW_NONDETERMINISTIC_RNG_RESUME=1` is explicitly authorized
and the non-bitwise lineage is recorded.

======================================================================
20. STUDENT POLICY, PURE-BC, DEF-MATERIALIZATION, AND BN SEMANTICS
======================================================================

The pure-BC update used to construct a PPO likelihood ratio even when its
coefficient was exactly zero.  A stale log probability around `-1e30` could
therefore overflow `exp(new_logp-old_logp)` and poison the nominally inactive
objective.  Permanently pure BC and scheduled coefficient-zero updates now
skip action log-probability and ratio construction completely, return an exact
zero surrogate, optimize the actor only from BC, and continue optimizing the
critic.  Hybrid updates still construct and use the PPO ratio.  Adaptive KL is
diagnostic-only in pure BC and actor-LR-active whenever PPO can contribute;
critic LR remains independent.

DeFM-style lazy encoders now expose `materialize_for_setup(device)`.  Actor,
critic, and strict teacher modules are materialized before schema validation,
broadcast, load, and optimizer creation.  Parameterless and buffer-only
device discovery is handled explicitly.  Frozen DeFM backbones override
`train()` so their BatchNorm layers remain in eval mode.  Any actor BatchNorm
that could update while PPO contributes is rejected; only frozen eval-mode BN
with running statistics is accepted.  The actual external DeFM source tree is
not installed in this workspace, so the real-backbone integration test is the
single expected skip; mocked lifecycle and optimizer-coverage tests pass.

