======================================================================
24. TEACHER/STUDENT ROLLOUT CONTRACT AND EXACT CONTINUATION CLOSURE
======================================================================

The active observation set is now derived from the objective that will
actually be collected at the current iteration.  The loaded teacher's real
perception input is included while teacher labels, teacher rollout control,
or fixed-BC capture need it, and is removed once the effective BC weight is
zero and PPO is the only objective.  Pure PPO therefore neither constructs,
resets, nor advances a teacher or teacher-only stochastic observation group.
The objective/schedule and active groups are prepared before the initial
canonical reset, including after resume, so that reset-time stateful/noisy
observations cannot be computed under a stale schedule.

Deterministic label modes now reject a Flow teacher with nonzero inference
noise; explicitly stochastic DAgger remains supported.  Strict teacher load
requires a valid actor config and an explicit normalization boolean, plus
normalizer epsilon when normalization is enabled.  Legacy teacher-MSE mode
rejects DAgger-only controls that it would otherwise ignore.  At PPO
coefficient one the BC/teacher path is not evaluated, while the PPO loss still
retains its coefficient.  A fixed-BC dataset that is still incomplete when
the DAgger weight reaches zero fails on every rank before entering pure PPO.
The startup noise cap now checks component and mean floors and cannot silently
violate either the configured cap or the policy's noise domain.

Full training resume is now exact-continuation-only: it requires both actor
and critic optimizer states and `load_optimizer=true`.  Resetting optimizer
moments or adaptive learning rates is a warm start and is rejected after all
preflight validation but before model/environment mutation.  The resume
preflight applies the same rule, while policy-init remains actor-only by
design.  PPO canonical checkpoint resets clear actor, critic, single-teacher,
and multi-teacher recurrent state.  The locomotion episode tracker snapshot
owns its CPU storage and its one-shot suppression guard is consumed exactly
once; restoring the adaptive snapshot after the forced reset does not arm it
again.  Frozen DeFM parameters are excluded from every gradient-reduction
payload.

Independent student-policy review verified the live r21 schemas directly:
