27. LOCOMOTION PENALTY-CURRICULUM SCIENTIFIC CORRECTNESS
======================================================================

`PenaltyCurriculum.reset()` previously ignored `env_ids`.  `BaseTask` calls
all manager reset hooks on every control step, including with an empty reset
selection, so the penalty scale was changing every step even when no episode
ended.  Both the stateful and legacy penalty paths now return on `None` or an
empty selection and change scale only for an actual reset batch.

The distributed locomotion synchronizer previously broadcast only
`env.reward_penalty_scale`, which is a logging mirror; it did not update the
authoritative term or the live reward weights.  It now broadcasts the
authoritative scale in float64 and atomically realigns
`PenaltyCurriculum.current_scale`, every `original_weight * scale` reward
configuration, the environment mirror, and `log_dict`.  Legacy state receives
the same treatment.  A requested multi-rank sync without an initialized
process group fails rather than silently continuing.

PPO cannot make a rank-local adaptive penalty objective scientific merely by
synchronizing at rollout boundaries: terminations inside the multi-step
rollout can make ranks use different reward weights.  PPO therefore rejects
multi-rank penalty curricula with nonzero degree.  Degree zero and single-rank
training remain valid.  FastSAC is not globally rejected because it
synchronizes before every sampled environment step, now using the corrected
authoritative synchronization.

Penalty configuration now requires explicit booleans, a nonempty tag, finite
scales/thresholds/degree, ordered nonnegative bounds and thresholds, and
`0 <= degree < 1`.  Enabled curricula must match at least one active reward;
all original and full-range derived weights are validated before any live
reward mutation.  The legacy public entry point shares the same contract.
The episode-average horizon must also be finite and positive.  State restore
uses one scale-application path so a canonical restore cannot leave the log
at a temporary reset value while the real objective has already reverted.
The full curriculum/WBT unit file passed 45 tests and the combined regression
passed 470 tests.

