46. TRAINING-STEP SYNCHRONIZATION REDUCTION (WORKSPACE CANDIDATE)
======================================================================

At 2026-07-16 UTC the reviewed documentation baseline was committed and
pushed to `origin/main` as `7914b196` before any performance work began.  The
active r22 formal run continues from its immutable source snapshot; none of
the workspace changes below can alter its code, environment or processes.

Read-only phase timing showed that the 64-minibatch training step spent most
of its time in fixed-latency collectives rather than actor/critic arithmetic.
The workspace candidate therefore removes the post-reduction standalone
gradient-finite scan and scalar verdict.  Actor and critic clipping remain
separate and continue to use `clip_grad_norm_(error_if_nonfinite=True)`;
their existing synchronized failure verdict still completes before either
optimizer may mutate state.  This preserves finite-gradient and fail-closed
semantics while removing one parameter scan and one all-rank collective from
each minibatch.

For the production `HOLOSOMA_CONTIGUOUS_MINIBATCHES=1` path, all local DAgger
valid counts are now computed from the same time-major slices as the rollout
generator and reduced as one short vector per iteration.  Each minibatch
receives its exact global boolean presence marker together with the existing
rollout-wide denominator.  Pure-BC all-empty minibatches therefore still skip
the actor optimizer on every rank, remote-only valid minibatches still step on
every rank, the critic behavior is unchanged, and distributed-loss weights
remain part of the global-presence definition.  Randomized/recurrent paths
retain the old per-minibatch fallback instead of changing their RNG or batch
ordering.

For the active 64-minibatch protocol this changes the small-collective count
from 451 to 324 per iteration: 127 fewer, or 28.2%.  Applying the measured
r22 phase costs predicts roughly 2.1 seconds less training time
(`11.46 s -> about 9.35 s`) and total iteration time near 15.7 seconds, but
these are pre-canary estimates rather than claimed production measurements.

The focused CPU regression passed 420 PPO core/student-step tests.  Adjacent
PPO schedule, DAgger/distill, fixed-BC, checkpoint-resume and rollout-storage
coverage added 157 passes, for 577 passing tests and zero failures.  A real
NaN backward-gradient test confirms both model parameters and both optimizer
states remain unchanged when clipping rejects the update.  A simulated
two-rank presence test confirms that the complete contiguous plan performs
one vector reduction and handles a locally empty but remotely valid
minibatch.  No GPU test, profiler attachment, source deployment or live-job
mutation was performed.

