55. EXACT OBSERVATION BASE-TERM REUSE AND R6 24-RANK ACCEPTANCE
======================================================================

The active AS observation configuration contained 39 base-term calls but only
20 unique audited computations.  Nineteen calls were exact duplicates,
including repeated base velocities, joint state, actions, motion command,
reference orientation and object pose/target/size terms.  The observation
manager now supports a default-off, same-`compute()` raw-result cache.  Reuse
requires all three conditions: the AS configuration explicitly opts in, the
term has empty params, and the function carries an explicit deterministic,
read-only, no-RNG decorator.  Stateful or unmarked terms are never cached.
Noise, scaling, clipping, history, concatenation and consumer order remain
independent and unchanged, and no value survives across environment steps.

Focused tests cover double opt-in/fail-closed params, call counts, noisy output
and RNG-state bitwise equality, history and subset reset, preview mode, active
groups, ephemeral lifetime and view/clone isolation.  The new tests plus
