======================================================================
57. EXACT CONTACT/ROLLOVER HOST-SYNC FIXES AND LAUNCHER SEMANTICS
======================================================================

Two exact collection-path fixes are retained.  In reward `wbt.py`, simulator
body-name resolution now caches both the immutable host-name tuple and the
device index tensor.  Object-contact rewards no longer execute
`selected_indexes.detach().cpu().tolist()` every control step merely to
reconstruct names already known on the host.  For the active 24-step rollout
this removes 24 device-to-host synchronization points per rank, or 576
rank-local synchronization points per 24-rank iteration, without changing the
selected bodies or downstream contact-force tensor.  The new
`test_object_contact_reward_hotpath.py` covers cache identity, missing/empty
selection failures and output semantics.

In command `wbt.py`, the standard episodic `motion_ends` contract now skips a
provably empty per-step `torch.where/nonzero` rollover path.  The fast path is
fail-closed: it applies only when the canonical termination manager owns the
clip end, motion-end reset is enabled and timeout/custom-wrapper ambiguity is
absent.  Continuing execution, custom terms, missing metadata and disabled
motion-end reset retain the original rollover implementation.
`test_motion_clip_rollover_contract.py` covers both the accepted and fallback
paths.

An attempted deferral of PPO rollout finite checks was rejected.  A two-rank
fault injection showed that a rank-local Python construction error could make
its peer wait until timeout if the synchronized verdict was deferred.  The
patch was exactly reverted.  The final PPO still performs the synchronized
per-step finite/error envelope before `env.step`; two-rank NaN and construction
fault probes made both ranks exit in approximately 2--11 ms without timeout,
and the 432-test PPO regression passed.

`batch_ne.sh` now owns and seals two previously ambient physics settings before
snapshot/remote execution:

  * `HOLOSOMA_OBJECT_COLLIDER_TYPE`, default `convex_decomposition`, accepting
    only `convex_decomposition` or `convex_hull`;
  * `HOLOSOMA_ACTIVATE_OBJECT_CONTACT_SENSORS`, canonical default `0`.

Both values are cleared from ambient node state, exported in the authenticated
payload and logged.  Invalid/default/candidate launcher contract cases pass.
The focused collection/PPO regression passed 481 tests; runtime asset and
provenance coverage passed 175 tests; `bash -n`, focused launcher cases and
`git diff --check` passed.

