======================================================================
64. R26 STUDENT-LEARNING FAILURE AND TRUTHFUL W&B TERMINATION
======================================================================

The three r26 jobs did not complete their 40,000-update target.  All three
were deliberately stopped by the fixed-BC guard at iteration 5101 after three
consecutive post-ramp evaluations exceeded the absolute 0.160 mu-MSE cap.
The 4900/5000/5100 values were respectively:

  ball    0.380256 / 0.378425 / 0.374865
  bin     0.330505 / 0.328691 / 0.325596
  barrel  0.283579 / 0.285706 / 0.288165

This was not a simulator, Gloo, CUDA, OOM, Xid or worker-liveness failure.
At the first positive PPO tier at step 700, diagnostic KL was approximately
1286/1763/1903 for ball/bin/barrel and the adaptive scheduler immediately
reduced the shared actor LR from 1e-3 to its 1e-5 floor.  Because the same
optimizer and LR serve both PPO and BC, the trust-region response also
throttled subsequent imitation learning.  The current online DAgger path
trains only the latest student-rollout batch; it does not aggregate a replay
dataset.  Offline recomputation on the authenticated terminal ball checkpoint
matched its fixed MSE to 7e-7, while a fresh AdamW optimizer fitted the same
frozen data below 0.16 in 25 steps and to 0.0387 in 500 steps.  Capacity,
forward/backward and loss scaling are therefore functional; the reproduced
failure is the online distribution/hybrid transition and forgetting regime.

The old code called wandb.finish() without an exit code even after the guard
raised, so W&B labeled all three terminated runs as `finished`.  The finalizer
now requires an explicit non-negative exit code and every success/error/final
cleanup path supplies the authoritative result.  The focused W&B suite passed
46 tests, py_compile and git diff --check.  The new source snapshot differs
from r26 in exactly train_agent.py and its W&B startup/cleanup unit test; an
rsync checksum comparison found no other executable-source change.

