4xheno9a all ended in the truthful `failed` state at step 900 rather than the
old misleading `finished` state.  Each run published a regular 92.55 MB
diagnostic_fixed_bc_guard_00901.pt.  Their SHA256 values were respectively:

  5fe9e361a29c341ac934d43ee342805e343eaaa52ebdf9c4b9bae76ba25aa358
  ddff7f34e385512459de72fa0a5d13a2daa6d6d652348a2c6831c8ab78b48475
  678ff01df230f4ca84efb02ebd96a482efdbb3b1c31a38670f98545841d0bb86

After proving W&B/checkpoint finalization, only the exact three launch
identities were closed.  The modern lifecycle controller returned rc=0 for
all three and released only their token-bound reservation pairs.  Final
checks on 10.99.0.167, 10.99.0.141 and 10.99.0.165 found zero GPU compute
applications, zero matching tmux sessions and zero listeners on 30911/30912,
30921/30922 and 30941/30942.  No unrelated process or job was controlled.

The code audit found that the internal `dagger` path is VideoMimic-style
current-occupancy BC, not classic dataset aggregation: after 16 minibatches it
clears the only rollout storage and never rehearses earlier teacher-labelled
student states.  The frozen fixed set is evaluation-only.  This exactly
matches the observed learn-then-forget trajectory, especially ball/barrel,
but it is not the only limitation.

An authenticated offline test reconstructed the exact r26 ball fixed dataset
and deterministic student mean network.  Starting from the terminal policy,
a stratified 80/20 split reached held-out MSE .148568 after 25 updates and
.089143 after 500; leaving rank 7 out reached .154866 and .132605.  This
proves the network, MSE scale, backward path and same-distribution capacity can
cross .160.  A harder fresh-random four-fold protocol trained on six complete
rank strata and held out two.  Full-depth train/test MSE averaged
.120101/.182170 after 500 updates, versus .121136/.185141 without depth.  The
four full-depth held-out results were .190063, .191177, .178060 and .169378.
These are operating points, not a Bayes lower bound, but they show that fitting
the all-rank sentinel does not prove generalization to a new camera/RNG/phase
stratum.

The observability audit explains that gap.  The teacher receives a 175-D
privileged actor observation including the full target joint trajectory and
exact object state; the student receives 94 low-dimensional values plus one
noisy/latent depth frame and has neither clip phase nor temporal history.  Its
contact-aware root command is exactly zero in 94.92% of the authenticated
fixed rows.  In addition, at least 67 teacher input dimensions are independently
noised each step even though teacher actions are deterministic means.  The
student camera independently has 3/4-frame latency, pose randomization,
holes/dropout and additive/multiplicative noise.  Action-space, clipping,
normalization, stochastic-teacher and pre/post-step alignment mismatches were
separately ruled out.

The next scientific Stage-1 therefore needs a bounded deterministic replay
buffer disjoint from the fixed gate, exact checkpoint/resume state, and a true
supervised actor-only objective.  A deployable pickup command plus the already
used drop command, temporal history and deterministic teacher-label A/B must
be evaluated explicitly; clip phase remains diagnostic-only.  No r27 actor is
eligible for PPO initialization.

======================================================================
67. R28 BOUNDED DAGGER REPLAY AND THREE INDEPENDENT WS8 RUNS
======================================================================

R27 established that removing PPO/KL interference was necessary but not
sufficient: all three pure-BC students still forgot earlier student-occupancy
states and missed the predeclared fixed-set gate.  R28 therefore implements a
bounded rank-local DAgger reservoir that is default-off and is admitted by the
formal launcher only for an operationally zero-PPO, unit-BC, no-std-matching
Stage-1.  It stores raw current-rollout student observations and deterministic
teacher means only after the all-rank fixed-BC dataset has been frozen.  Each
rank uses an independent CPU generator and Algorithm R reservoir sampling;
current and replay losses are combined as `(1-f)*current + f*replay` with the
same global weighted denominator semantics as distributed BC.  Full resume
restores each rank's buffer, counters, generator state and fixed-set binding;
actor-only policy initialization deliberately clears that lineage.

The supervised path now has a true actor-only optimizer step: PPO surrogate,
value and entropy objectives are operationally zero, the critic receives no
optimizer update, and the ordinary all-rank weight-consistency checks remain
enabled.  The launcher also makes the PPO controller explicit rather than
accepting ambient defaults: schedule=fixed, desired_KL=0.01, actor/critic
initial LR=1e-3 and bounds=[1e-5,1e-2].  Resume preflight canonicalizes only
legacy implicit-None LR bounds and continues to reject real schema or recipe
drift.  Focused validation passed 428 PPO/replay tests, 98 resume tests and 78
train-CLI tests; the replay and LR launcher contracts and independent archive
diff audit also passed.  The previously found single-rank replay denominator
bug was fixed without changing the already-correct eight-rank branch.

