======================================================================
80. DEBUG REPLAY PRODUCER/ARTIFACT FAIL-CLOSED CONTRACT
======================================================================

The first exact replay attempt exposed a launcher false-success path.  The
video recorder intentionally catches an exception in its recording thread and
does not interrupt the main thread; when zero frames remain, its encoder also
returns without publishing a file.  Consequently replay.py can exit zero after
printing a traceback, while the previous debug_as_replay_record.sh trusted only
that exit status and incorrectly printed Completed.

The debug launcher now fingerprints the target directory before each producer
invocation and, after a zero exit status, requires exactly one newly created or
changed MP4.  That artifact must be a non-symlink, non-empty regular file and
ffprobe must decode a positive-size video stream containing at least one frame.
Producer failure, no artifact, a stale artifact, multiple changed artifacts,
or an invalid artifact therefore cannot be reported as successful.  This is a
launcher-only working-tree repair; it does not alter the frozen b39f source or
any live job.

A CPU-only launcher regression covers a nonzero producer, an exit-zero producer
with no MP4, an exit-zero producer with a corrupt MP4, and a valid two-frame
MP4.  Independent reruns passed bash syntax, the complete regression,
shellcheck, and targeted git diff checks.  The code and test remain unstaged;
the staged allowlist is still exactly agent.md plus this review log.

