======================================================================
82. EXTERNAL-AS CLOSURE, MANDATORY GPU-IDLE GATES, AND FINAL REGRESSION
======================================================================

The corrected single-ball launch on 10.99.0.117 exposed a real formal-launch
gap: the selected immutable motion/map existed, but the external base URDF was
missing on the target.  Replay and W&B verification had already completed, and
the old preflight did not discover the missing dependency until the target
wrapper ran immediately before torchrun.  The transaction failed closed and
released its exact session and rendezvous reservations, but a formal launch
must reject this condition before any W&B/lifecycle mutation.  This was the
production reason for the external-AS closure work below; it was not merely a
test-hardening exercise.

`batch_ne.sh` now performs a complete external-AS barrier on every target from
the authenticated source snapshot.  The barrier binds the exact selected
motion NPZ, object map, URDF and recursively referenced mesh bytes, solid
selection/contact data, single-slot source/view, and source-derived rank plan.
All nodes must report identical path, digest, and world-size identities before
W&B replay verification, intent publication, port reservation, or tmux.  The
generated train control seals those values, and the real solid/perception
entrypoints revalidate them immediately before worker entry.  A manifest can
no longer authenticate a rank plan merely by describing itself: publication
and current verification both derive the expected plan from the immutable
source closure.

The selected-GPU idle check is now a mandatory two-boundary contract.  An
early, read-only `nvidia-smi` probe runs before heavy asset/runtime work for
`prepare`, `all`, and `launch`; it uses only the resolved stdlib Python and
cannot import torch, create lifecycle state, start tmux, or initialize W&B.
After optional node health/contact checks, `launch` repeats the same selected
GPU probe immediately before staging and worker creation.  Consequently
`SKIP_NODE_HEALTH_CHECK=1` skips only the optional health bundle and can never
skip either mandatory idle gate.  A busy or malformed selected GPU set fails
before consuming the requested cards.

Published source/view/rank namespaces are mode-sealed (`0444` regular files,
`0555` directories) and rechecked across publication, all-node barrier,
control execution, and wrapper entry.  The migration path correctly thaws an
older v3 mode-only tree only while exchanging its namespace, then reseals it.
Output roots and all relevant ancestors are checked lexically so a symlink or
non-directory cannot redirect validation or publication outside the intended
tree.  The replay producer was also made fail-closed: exit zero is accepted
only when exactly one new/changed non-symlink, non-empty MP4 is published and
ffprobe confirms a decodable positive-frame video stream.

The dynamic launcher fixture was repaired without changing production order.
Optional node-health failure and mandatory pre-launch-idle failure now use
separate injection points and independently prove exact rollback before tmux.
The repeated generic lifecycle cases use a temporary, content-closed one-clip
box28 external bank, reducing each closure-heavy case from about 127 seconds
to roughly 6--13 seconds.  The dedicated contract still exercises the real
r29 Rule-90 v2 motion/map/URDF/mesh closure and all three digests, so this
fixture optimization does not replace production-scale coverage.  A final
test-only failure was traced to an obsolete dry-run prefix assertion: the
mandatory probe uses `bounded-ssh`, not the older bare `ssh` label.  Independent
reproduction proved exactly one bounded early probe, zero transfers, and the
expected local SHA rejection; the assertion was corrected accordingly.

