1. `train_object_generalist_ds.sh` validated contact sidecars using runtime
   default-pose prepend compensation but did not pass that semantic into the
   live `MotionCommand` CLI or pure-RL provenance. The launcher now parses the
   boolean strictly, rejects a conflicting raw CLI override, requires the
   offline-contact/default-prepend combination to agree, records it in
   provenance, and passes
   `contact-interval-runtime-prepend-compensation=True` to the live command.
   `scripts/compute_training_provenance.py`,
   `src/holosoma/holosoma/utils/training_provenance.py`, and tests were updated
   consistently. Shell syntax, Python compilation, and the relevant 142-test
   combination passed.
2. During the first formal distributed preflight, the launcher failed closed
   because `HOLOSOMA_MOTION_SHARD_MANIFEST` was revalidated by each worker but
   was omitted from controller-side `compute_training_provenance.py`. The
   launcher now derives the exact manifest from
   `HOLOSOMA_RANK_LOCAL_MOTION_ROOT` when needed, requires it to exist,
   canonicalizes/exports it, and passes `--motion-shard-manifest`. The new
   regression `test_generalist_rank_shard_manifest_matches_worker_revalidation`
   and the complete targeted launcher file (8 tests) passed. A dry run then
   proved controller and worker both selected
   `8bb025b05d6028f3d85c133b8e10ba19ddb54e80b77e8f54ff1f123fed6d5175`.
3. The node wrapper's UECC query used an unsupported short field alias on the
   installed NVIDIA driver. It was corrected before formal workers to use
   `ecc.errors.uncorrected.volatile.total`; all 64 twice-sampled selected-GPU
   gates subsequently reported zero memory, utilization, applications, and
   uncorrectable ECC.

