[2026-07-24] coupled object static/dynamic friction sampling

Replaced independent object static/dynamic friction sampling with the exact
contract `static ~ Uniform(0.1,0.7)`,
`ratio ~ Uniform(0.7,0.99)`, and `dynamic = static * ratio`. The resulting
dynamic-friction support is [0.07,0.693], every bucket has
`0.7 <= dynamic/static <= 0.99`, and there is no point mass at ratio one.
Object restitution remains independently Uniform(0,1). Robot material
randomization and its existing independent ranges are unchanged.

The implementation preserves IsaacLab's 64 startup material buckets and its
original three uniform RNG draws. IsaacLab samples the second bucket column
from the ratio range, then HoloSoma converts it to `static * ratio` before the
standard material assignment. This consumes no additional RNG and does not
create one unique PhysX material per environment. Environments/shapes still
select randomly among the 64 coupled buckets.

The new path validates all ranges and bucket values before assignment, rejects
ambiguous simultaneous legacy dynamic-range and new ratio-range parameters,
and fails closed if the installed IsaacLab randomizer no longer exposes the
bucket tensor. After assignment it reads the actual PhysX material buffer and
verifies every observed dynamic/static ratio against [0.7,0.99]; a mismatch
raises before training, while a successful startup logs the observed ratio
minimum and maximum.

Both object randomization presets, with and without action delay, were read
back with exact config values static=[0.1,0.7], ratio=[0.7,0.99] and
restitution=[0,1], with no independent dynamic-friction range. Python
compilation and whitespace checks passed. The focused suite reported
18 passed and covers distribution bounds/means, invalid inputs, IsaacLab
bucket replacement, assignment invocation, PhysX readback, config provenance,
category mass, and coupled mass/full-inertia contracts.

This change affects only future fresh simulator startup; existing PhysX
materials cannot be hot-updated through this config edit. No live training
job was attached, paused, stopped, or modified, and no GPU simulator or W&B
write was used. Code and tests remain unstaged; only `agent.md` and this log
are allowed in the Git index.

